SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Joint Meeting of the Council on Economic and Fiscal Policy and the Council of New Form of Capitalism Realization","publisher":"Prime Minister's Office of Japan","publication_date":"2022-06-07","url":"https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/actions/202206/_00020.html","claim":"Kishida said the government had finalized the Grand Design and Action Plan for a New Form of Capitalism and would implement concrete multi-year plans for startups, green transformation, and measures to double asset income.","locator":"lines 39-51, Prime Minister's remarks after the joint meeting","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary PMO transcript with explicit policy-finalization language and implementation commitments.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022, at the point the policy package was finalized.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Kishida as prime minister chairing and announcing the package; execution still depended on the cabinet and line ministries.","contrary_evidence":["This is a commitment and design document, not evidence of delivery by itself.","Later outcome data still show mixed results under inflation pressure."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.6","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Startup Development Portal Site","publisher":"Cabinet Secretariat, Government of Japan","publication_date":"2022-11-28","url":"https://www.cas.go.jp/jp/seisaku/su-portal/index.html","claim":"The government says it decided the Startup Development Five-year Plan on November 28, 2022 and will push the three pillars of human capital and network building, funding and exit diversification, and open innovation as one package.","locator":"intro paragraph on the portal landing page","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Cabinet Secretariat portal explicitly states the decision date, the plan name, and the policy pillars.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and tied to the Kishida cabinet's policy timetable.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Kishida's cabinet agenda; downstream execution still depended on agencies, firms, and local implementers.","contrary_evidence":["The portal describes intended execution rather than measured outcomes.","Startup targets are ambitious and do not by themselves show success."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.6","8B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"FY2022 (April 2022-March 2023) Annual Report","publisher":"Japan Fair Trade Commission","publication_date":"2023-06-16","url":"https://www.jftc.go.jp/en/about_jftc/annual_reports/2022.html","claim":"In FY2022 the JFTC opened 116 antimonopoly investigations and took 11 legal measures, including eight cease-and-desist orders and three commitment plan approvals.","locator":"Section 2.1.2-2.1.3 of the annual report","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary regulator annual report with quantified enforcement statistics for the relevant fiscal year.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Covers FY2022, overlapping the 2022 ruler period.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but material: the JFTC is an independent regulator, yet its enforcement and advocacy posture reflects the government framework Kishida was using.","contrary_evidence":["This shows institutional enforcement capacity more than direct personal direction from Kishida.","It does not isolate which cases, if any, were uniquely Kishida-driven."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.5","8B.6","8B.9"]}
